From: Daniele Masato <daniele.masato@pm.me>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: use DMA on the Sophgo CV18xx

The CV18xx DWC2 reports DMA and descriptor DMA support (GHWCFG), and the
vendor 5.10 kernel runs it with g_dma = 1 and g_dma_desc = 1. Mainline's
dwc2_set_cv1800_params() forces PIO, which moves every USB byte with the
CPU and costs the single core the FIFO refill interrupts. Drop the
override so both modes come from the hardware parameters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -225,7 +225,6 @@
 	p->otg_caps.hnp_support = false;
 	p->otg_caps.srp_support = false;
 	p->host_dma = false;
-	p->g_dma = false;
 	p->speed = DWC2_SPEED_PARAM_HIGH;
 	p->phy_type = DWC2_PHY_TYPE_PARAM_UTMI;
 	p->phy_utmi_width = 16;
